- run it in continuous integration (for example GitHub Actions or GitLab CI) and in containers;
- call it from your own programs and scripts, whatever their licence;
- redistribute the unmodified archive or binary as part of a container image, a continuous
  integration image, a virtual machine image or an installation script, provided that this LICENSE
  and THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt go with it and that you do not charge for paginel-text itself.

You may not:

- modify, decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer paginel-text, except where the law allows it
  notwithstanding this restriction;
- sell, rent, lend or sublicense paginel-text, distribute it on its own as a product of yours, or
  distribute modified copies;
- remove or change its copyright and licence notices.

The documents you make with paginel-text are yours: the author claims no right on them.

The documentation and the examples of this repository (the docs/ and examples/ folders) are under
the MIT No Attribution licence: see docs/LICENSE and examples/LICENSE.

No warranty. paginel-text is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranty of any kind,
express or implied, to the extent permitted by law: in particular no warranty of merchantability,
of fitness for a particular purpose, of non-infringement, of accuracy of the documents it produces,
or that it will run without errors or interruption. You alone choose to use it and check what it
produces before you rely on it. The author has no obligation to provide support, maintenance,
corrections or new versions, and may change or stop paginel-text at any time.

No liability. To the extent permitted by law, the author shall not be liable for any damage, direct
or indirect, arising from the use of paginel-text or from the inability to use it, including loss
or corruption of data or documents, loss of profit, business interruption or claims of third
parties, even if advised of the possibility of such damage.

The third-party components that paginel-text includes (libraries, fonts) keep their own licences:
see THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt in each archive.

Because this repository is public, GitHub's Terms of Service let other GitHub users view it and copy
("fork") it on GitHub.

